# oracle: pair sdpd/taitwater/isothermal in 2d (random thermal forces) cut down from examples/PACKAGES/dpd-smooth/2d-diffusion/in.lammps: a 10x10 square block of fluid particles (100 atoms, box -0.5..0.5) with no solid disk (fix rigid/meso is not in the engine), enforce2d, 20 steps; thermo and per-atom state compared
# measured max error vs native (per atom, relative to max(1,|value|)): 2.8e-17 (atom 4 vx), the random thermal forces included; thermo agrees at 1e-8.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
dimension       2
units           micro
atom_style      sph
variable        a equal 0.1
variable        L equal 0.5
variable        T equal 300.
variable        rho_0 equal 1.
variable        c_0 equal 100.
variable        mu equal 1.
variable        h equal $a*4.5
variable        mass equal $a*$a*$a*${rho_0}
variable        dt equal 1e-3
variable        skin equal 0.2*$h
region          box block -$L $L -$L $L -0.5 0.5 units box
create_box      1 box
lattice         sq $a
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * ${mass}
set             group all sph/rho ${rho_0}
pair_style      sdpd/taitwater/isothermal $T ${mu} 76787
pair_coeff      * * ${rho_0} ${c_0} ${h}
fix             1 all sph
fix             2 all enforce2d
neighbor        ${skin} bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes
timestep        ${dt}
thermo_style    custom step time pe ke etotal
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             20
